{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/309751-first-principles-basic-refinements","id":309751,"title":"First Principles: Basic Refinements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-11T19:38:37-08:00","id":309751,"title":"First Principles: Basic Refinements","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/first-principles-basic-refinements/\" target=\"_blank\">And here ya go, ya wonderful people.</a><br /> <br /> To the Devs: Thank you for Ila, I\u2019ve always wanted to know if there could be a Promethean digital AI (she isn\u2019t now, but she was for a while). Also, her origin is hilarious (congrats, you\u2019ve passed the Turing Test! Too bad it\u2019s because the computer now <i>exactly</i> imitates a human, right down to the self-awareness and sapience).<br /> Also, I like the idea some Furies became that way in an attempt to avoid losing what sanity and compassion they had left, or by barging back on to the Pilgrimage, all guns blazing. Shows the positive sides of it, even though they\u2019re by default the dark side of the ostensibly human-seeking Refinements","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-12-2014, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T19:50:27-08:00","id":309769,"title":"","content":"Okay, <i>now</i> I want to hear about demiurges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T20:19:59-08:00","id":309808,"title":"","content":"I have an idea, that is definitely not something that should be a canon norm, as many tables would find it far too restrictive, but would really reinforce the association between following a Refinement and alchemically changing oneself for those tables that want to play that up.<br /> <br /> Basically some Transmutations can only be bought while following their associated Refinement.<br /> <br /> Corporeum, Deception, Disquietism, Senorium, &amp; Vulcanus can all be bought by any Promethean, though only at the favored rate by one on their associated Refinement.<br /> <br /> Alchemicus, Benefice, Contamination, Electrification, Luciferus, Mesmerism, Metamorphosis, Saturninus, Spiritus, Vitalus can only be bought while following their associated Refinement.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, each Lineage has an associated restricted Transmutation type they may purchase even while not following the associated Refinement, though only paying the discounted rated while following said Refinement...<br /> <br /> Frankenstein: Electrification<br /> Galatea: Mesmerism<br /> Osiris: Alchemicus<br /> Tammuz: (we don't know exactly what they'll be like in 2nd Edition yet, I'm going to go with Metamorphosis for now, but that may change)<br /> Ulgan: Spiritus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T20:34:55-08:00","id":309837,"title":"","content":"Ila tho.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">characterlimit</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T20:44:24-08:00","id":309843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/309751-first-principles-basic-refinements?p=309808#post309808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea, that is definitely not something that should be a canon norm, as many tables would find it far too restrictive, but would really reinforce the association between following a Refinement and alchemically changing oneself for those tables that want to play that up.<br /> <br /> Basically some Transmutations can only be bought while following their associated Refinement.<br /> <br /> Corporeum, Deception, Disquietism, Senorium, &amp; Vulcanus can all be bought by any Promethean, though only at the favored rate by one on their associated Refinement.<br /> <br /> Alchemicus, Benefice, Contamination, Electrification, Luciferus, Mesmerism, Metamorphosis, Saturninus, Spiritus, Vitalus can only be bought while following their associated Refinement.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, each Lineage has an associated restricted Transmutation type they may purchase even while not following the associated Refinement, though only paying the discounted rated while following said Refinement...<br /> <br /> Frankenstein: Electrification<br /> Galatea: Mesmerism<br /> Osiris: Alchemicus<br /> Tammuz: (we don't know exactly what they'll be like in 2nd Edition yet, I'm going to go with Metamorphosis for now, but that may change)<br /> Ulgan: Spiritus</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I was just about to post something along these lines. You missed a Lineage, though: the Unfleshed. And despite the traditional association between Frankenstein and lightning, I\u2019d feel far more comfortable associating Electrification with the Unfleshed than with the Wretched. For them, I\u2019d be more likely to go with Vitalus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T07:13:58-08:00","id":310219,"title":"","content":"You're actually not far off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T08:39:50-08:00","id":310270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/309751-first-principles-basic-refinements?p=309837#post309837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ila tho.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">characterlimit</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the correction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T13:07:15-08:00","id":310475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/309751-first-principles-basic-refinements?p=309843#post309843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was just about to post something along these lines. You missed a Lineage, though: the Unfleshed. And despite the traditional association between Frankenstein and lightning, I\u2019d feel far more comfortable associating Electrification with the Unfleshed than with the Wretched. For them, I\u2019d be more likely to go with Vitalus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being animated by lightning is one of the core elements for the Wretched, more so than the Unfleshed being modern robots, which is far from universal. I'm waiting till we know more about the Unfleshed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T17:28:42-08:00","id":310748,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a Promethean's powers being somewhat representative of where their Pilgrimage has taken them, and tying them to the Refinements is certainly one way to do that.<br /> <br /> Another thing to take from this is that Stannus is still the &quot;default state&quot; of a Promethean. I was hoping that each Lineage might have a different Refinement to revert to, based in part on their prevailing humour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T15:28:07-08:00","id":314853,"title":"","content":"After reading those posts about the Refinements, my troupe have taken to calling the two types Base Refinements and Noble Refinements, which is funny if you know much about how those terms are used in alchemy. The Refinement of Gold is a Base Refinement, but Gold is often portrayed as the acme of Noble Materials in Western Alchemy, after all.<br /> <br /> I put it out as an idea that I doubt shall make it into <b>Promethean</b> Second Edition. However, beyond the tongue-in-cheek irony of it, I wonder if such distinctions could be reflections of Azothic Memory, and if some very studious Created might use that as cause to wonder if the Principle has a sense of humour? I mean, beyond its sense for Humours... And yeah, I may have neither one of those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}